**/.return-meta.json
# The .claude/ deploy tree is a disposable build artifact regenerated from the
# source store in agent-system/extensions/ (selection pinned by the project-root
# .claude-extensions.json). Nothing under it is hand-authored — every deployed
# file has a source, enforced by the check-extension-docs.sh hard gate — so it is
# not tracked. Wipe and regenerate from the <leader>al picker at any time.
/.claude/
# Runtime logs relocated out of .claude/.opencode so they survive a wipe (see
# agent-system/extensions/core/docs/architecture/extension-system.md)
**/.agent-logs/
# Staging directory for the settings.json/settings.local.json backup/restore
# wrapper (settings_backup.lua) used across a full .claude/.opencode wipe.
/.claude-settings-backup/
/.opencode-settings-backup/
/specs/tmp
# /.claude/tmp/ is covered by the blanket /.claude/ rule above
/.opencode/tmp/
**/.postflight-pending
**/.git-snapshot-marker
# Ephemeral orchestration session state: per-dispatch scratch, mutex directories,
# and loop guards. All are runtime-only — each is overwritten or removed within a
# single orchestrate run (see .claude/docs/architecture/handoff-schema.md, which
# specifies .orchestrator-handoff.json as "runtime; not checked in" and overwritten
# every dispatch cycle). They are ignored here because the postflight commit stage
# runs before its own marker-cleanup stage, so anything left unignored is swept into
# a commit mid-lifecycle.
**/.lock/
**/.orchestrator-handoff.json
**/.orchestrator-loop-guard
**/.continuation-loop-guard
**/.orchestrator-churn-state.json
**/.postflight-loop-guard
**/.orchestrator-multi-state.json
**/.return-meta-*.json
**/.events.lock
# Note: specs/events.jsonl is deliberately NOT ignored — it is an append-only durable
# store (see .claude/context/formats/events-format.md). Do not add it here.
.syncprotect
specs/literature/**/*.pdf
specs/literature/**/*.djvu
# Literature SQLite databases (ephemeral - rebuilt from chunk files)
.literature.db
.literature.db.tmp
specs/literature/.literature.db
specs/literature/.literature.db.tmp
# (.claude/scripts/literature-pyenv/ is covered by the blanket /.claude/ rule above)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
